{"version": 2, "width": 105, "height": 32, "timestamp": 1787203442, "idle_time_limit": 2.0, "env": {"SHELL": "/usr/bin/zsh", "TERM": ""}, "title": "cdk-cicd-wrapper v3 — where we are"}
[0.008699, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36m 1. Where this recording came from\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[1.511979, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# Every proof states its own provenance: which branch and commit, and whether\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[3.515927, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# the tree was clean when it was recorded.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[5.519914, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$ git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[6.525239, "o", "v3\r\n"]
[6.525438, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$ git rev-parse --short HEAD\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[7.530968, "o", "d07be53\r\n"]
[7.531168, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# An empty listing below means a clean tree.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[9.535133, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$ git status --porcelain | head\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[10.544966, "o", "?? docs/proof/where-we-are.cast\r\n?? test/proof/demos/lib/\r\n?? test/proof/demos/where-we-are.sh\r\n"]
[10.545294, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# The work so far, one commit per verified unit -- the evolution is reviewable.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[12.548999, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$ git log --oneline -4\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[13.564889, "o", "\u001b[33md07be53\u001b[m\u001b[33m (\u001b[m\u001b[1;36mHEAD\u001b[m\u001b[33m -> \u001b[m\u001b[1;32mv3\u001b[m\u001b[33m)\u001b[m feat: add v3 app-config layer (AppConfig accessor + loader)\r\n\u001b[33me3feb41\u001b[m test: add v3 fixture apps\r\n\u001b[33m7a4027a\u001b[m test: add v3 proof harness and narrated milestone recorder\r\n\u001b[33m6acdd69\u001b[m docs: add v3 design, task board and agent working notes\r\n"]
[13.565218, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36m 2. The v3 public surface (jsii-safe)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[13.565257, "o", "\u001b[1;36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[15.068814, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# v3 is additive: it hangs off the existing package entry point, so the published\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[17.072726, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# 0.x surface keeps working. Only a curated set of types crosses the jsii boundary.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[19.077483, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$ sed -n \"1,40p\" packages/@cdklabs/cdk-cicd-wrapper/src/v3/index.ts | grep -vE \"^//|^$\" | head -20\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[20.083597, "o", "export { AppConfig, AppConfigOptions } from './appconfig/accessor';\r\nexport { ConfigErrorKind } from './appconfig/error';\r\nexport { AwsEnvironment, BaseConfig, RemovalPolicies, RemovalPolicyValue } from './appconfig/schema';\r\nexport { ConditionalFieldGroup, ConfigSchema, FieldKind, RequiredField } from './appconfig/validation';\r\n"]
[20.084165, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# jsii SILENTLY drops exported free functions, so the machinery (the generic loader,\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[22.087879, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# the ConfigError class, the bare helpers) stays internal and only classes/structs/enums\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[24.09211, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# are exported. We verify that against the generated assembly rather than trusting it:\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[26.096349, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$ node -e 'const a=JSON.parse(require(\"fs\").readFileSync(\"packages/@cdklabs/cdk-cicd-wrapper/.jsii\",\"utf8\")); const v3=Object.keys(a.types).filter(k=>(a.types[k].locationInModule||{}).filename?.includes(\"src/v3\")); console.log(v3.length+\" v3 types in the assembly:\"); v3.forEach(k=>console.log(\"  \"+a.types[k].kind.padEnd(9)+\" \"+k.split(\".\").pop()));'\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[27.126445, "o", "11 v3 types in the assembly:\r\n  class     AppConfig\r\n"]
[27.126869, "o", "  interface AppConfigOptions\r\n  interface AwsEnvironment\r\n  interface BaseConfig\r\n  interface ConditionalFieldGroup\r\n  enum      ConfigErrorKind\r\n  interface ConfigSchema\r\n  enum      FieldKind\r\n  interface RemovalPolicies\r\n  enum      RemovalPolicyValue\r\n  interface RequiredField\r\n"]
[27.13279, "o", "\u001b[1;33m→ 11 types, and AppConfig is the one class a user actually calls.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[29.13685, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36m 3. M1: the config layer, through the API a user calls\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[30.641553, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# AppConfig.load reads a per-environment config file, layers the wrapper's base\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[32.645251, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# defaults under it, derives account/region from CDK's environment, and validates\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[34.649463, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# against a caller-supplied schema. First: JSON and YAML must load identically.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[36.653926, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$ node \"/home/gyalai/.workspace/src/cdk-cicd-wrapper/test/proof/demos/lib/appconfig-tour.js\" json-yaml-identical\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[37.904155, "o", "from JSON: {\"aws\":{\"accountId\":\"111111111111\",\"region\":\"us-west-2\"},\"tags\":{},\"removalPolicies\":{\"dynamoDBTable\":\"retain\",\"s3Bucket\":\"retain\"},\"application\":\"shop\"}\r\n"]
[37.904206, "o", "from YAML: {\"aws\":{\"accountId\":\"111111111111\",\"region\":\"us-west-2\"},\"tags\":{},\"removalPolicies\":{\"dynamoDBTable\":\"retain\",\"s3Bucket\":\"retain\"},\"application\":\"shop\"}\r\nidentical: true\r\n"]
[37.911041, "o", "\u001b[1;33m→ Same object either way -- the file format is the user's choice, not a behaviour change.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[39.915548, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36m 4. Safe-by-default merge + derived environment\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[41.41956, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# A blank aws block plus CDK's ambient account/region: the values are derived, and\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[43.42376, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# the base defaults RETAIN stateful resources so the wrapper never widens blast radius.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[45.428011, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$ node \"/home/gyalai/.workspace/src/cdk-cicd-wrapper/test/proof/demos/lib/appconfig-tour.js\" derived-account\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[46.675974, "o", "{\r\n  \"aws\": {\r\n    \"accountId\": \"111111111111\",\r\n    \"region\": \"eu-west-1\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"tags\": {},\r\n  \"removalPolicies\": {\r\n    \"dynamoDBTable\": \"retain\",\r\n    \"s3Bucket\": \"retain\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"application\": \"shop\"\r\n}\r\n"]
[46.682837, "o", "\u001b[1;33m→ removalPolicies default to retain; the account/region came from the environment.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[48.687197, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36m 5. Fails closed, with a typed error\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[50.191184, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# A missing required key does not deploy a half-config -- it throws a typed\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[52.194984, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# ConfigError, which at a CDK entry point makes cdk synth exit non-zero and emit\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[54.199166, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# no templates.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[56.203774, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$ node \"/home/gyalai/.workspace/src/cdk-cicd-wrapper/test/proof/demos/lib/appconfig-tour.js\" missing-key\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[57.437963, "o", "threw: ConfigError\r\n"]
[57.438177, "o", "kind:  MISSING_KEY (ConfigErrorKind.MISSING_KEY = MISSING_KEY)\r\nmessage: Missing or malformed required config key 'aws.accountId' in /tmp/appconfig-tour-hYGIfC/config.json (expected string)\r\n"]
[57.445085, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# And a subtle one: an unquoted 12-digit account id in YAML is a NUMBER. Coercing it\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[59.449233, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# would corrupt a leading-zero account, so it is rejected exactly like an absent key.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[61.453659, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$ node \"/home/gyalai/.workspace/src/cdk-cicd-wrapper/test/proof/demos/lib/appconfig-tour.js\" numeric-account\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[62.698757, "o", "threw: ConfigError / MISSING_KEY\r\n"]
[62.699088, "o", "message: Missing or malformed required config key 'aws.accountId' in /tmp/appconfig-tour-N0qjNt/config.yaml (expected string)\r\n"]
[62.705028, "o", "\u001b[1;33m→ Wrong type is treated the same as missing -- no silent coercion.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[64.709954, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36m 6. Wave 0: the teardown guard that makes real deploys safe\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[66.21421, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# Every later gate is a real deploy to a test account. Nothing is ever deleted\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[68.218136, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# unless this guard says the stack is ours -- right tag, right account, right region,\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[70.22206, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# and ambient credentials that also point at the test account. This runs the guard\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[72.225705, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# through 15 cases with a FAKE aws CLI, so it makes no real calls.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[74.230083, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$ DEMO_PAUSE=0 bash test/proof/harness.test.sh | tail -6\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[75.444446, "o", "  allowed    our own tagged stack                      guard: 'cdkcicdtest-rtest-level0' is ours (cdk-cicd-wrapper-test=rtest) in us-west-2 -- destroy allowed\r\n== destroy_stack consults the guard before deleting\r\n  no delete   untagged stack refused by destroy_stack FAIL: guard: refusing to destroy 'cdkcicdtest-rtest-level0' -- it does not carry the 'cdk-cicd-wrapper-test' tag\r\n  deleted     our own tagged stack via destroy_stack reached delete-stack\r\n\r\nPASS: 15/15 guard cases behaved as specified\r\n"]
[75.444856, "o", "\u001b[1;33m→ 15/15, including a case that fails if the delete is ever moved above the guard.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[77.448922, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36m 7. The M1 unit suite\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[78.952962, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# The config layer ships with its own unit suite -- 4 files under test/v3 -- run on\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[80.957078, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# every gate (60 passing, ~99% line coverage) and reviewed by an agent with mutation\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[82.96102, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# testing before commit. Here are the files and the test count, counted live:\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[84.964936, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$ ls -1 packages/@cdklabs/cdk-cicd-wrapper/test/v3/appconfig/\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[85.971093, "o", "accessor.test.ts\r\ndefaults.test.ts\r\nloader.test.ts\r\nvalidation.test.ts\r\n"]
[85.97133, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$ grep -rhcE \"^\\s*(test|it)\\(\" packages/@cdklabs/cdk-cicd-wrapper/test/v3/appconfig/*.test.ts | awk \"{n+=\\$1} END{print n\\\" test cases\\\"}\"\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[86.978288, "o", "60 test cases\r\n"]
[86.978609, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36mWhere we are: Wave 0 harness + M1 config layer done. Next: m1-verify, then M2 runtime injection + the first real-deploy demo.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
